  "notes": [
    "All three attempts create the swap chain and clear its back buffer, then receive DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED. No pixel oracle succeeds. The original display was explicitly awakened and visually checked before the first v38 attempt.",
    "Windows accepts both staging metadata queries. Entry/return breakpoints show that staging CreateAllocation returns STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER. The final trace establishes Resource=1 with zero resource-private metadata and one valid 40-byte allocation descriptor. The previous implementation incorrectly requires resource-private metadata for every resource-owned allocation.",
    "Revision adc280f permits this exact ownership form only for a single valid presentation staging allocation, creates a resource owner, and tests lifetime and malformed-input rejection. Live acceptance requires the next package.",
    "The first diagnostic allocation dump includes six DWORDs beyond the private descriptor; only its defined 40 bytes are interpreted. The final trace limits the metadata dump to ten DWORDs.",
    "The three completed fences are CPU clears. Neither accepted PresentCb statuses nor component NPU draws establish window delivery or desktop migration."
  ],
